WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:10.623
- My talk is on logical causal inference,

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:16.200
truth, counterfactual
scope, and invariance.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.740
So where is the...

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:25.010
Okay, in his webpage, Zenna Tavares

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.140
whose webpage I looked
at before this conference

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:32.370
says, "I want to understand
how humans reason,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.970
how they come to derive
knowledge from observing

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.030
and interacting with the world."

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.050
And this is also what
I want to understand.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.770
And in this talk I will
pursue this interest

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:51.390
by examining two types of
inference that are often thought

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.510
to be very different from each other.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.680
Logical inference and causal inference.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.930
Logical inference, allegedly,

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.660
has nothing to do with the world.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.660
Causal inference has everything
to do with the world.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:12.180
I will examine the nature
of these inferences

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.000
by using three parameters.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.000
One, truth in the strong
sense of factual truth

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.220
or truth in the world,
not linguistic truth

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:29.580
or coherentist truth, or pragmatist truth.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.810
And counterfactual scope, and invariance.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.810
My result will be one,
contrary to expectations,

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.840
logical and causal inferences are similar

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.930
with respect to truth in the world.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:50.930
Two, they are different with
respect to counterfactual scope

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.423
and invariance, but only in degree.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:56.963
Truth.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.020
Logic is usually thought
to have nothing to do

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:05.190
with the world, hence
with truth in the world.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:10.190
Logic is said to be analytic,
i.e. based on language

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.560
or meaning regardless of how the world

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.030
happens to be or necessarily is.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.880
The logical inference, and here I use same

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.880
kind of inference as Alex,
one, Pa or Pb, not Pa,

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:33.210
therefore Pb is of the same kind

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.210
as the linguistic inference,

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:40.950
A is a bachelor, therefore A is unmarried.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:45.600
And different in kind from
Hume's relevant example

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.670
of a causal inference.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.760
A hit B, therefore B moved,

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.573
where A and B are say, billiard balls.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:00.933
Now influence three, A
hit B, therefore B moves,

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.257
depends on the way the world is

00:03:04.257 --> 00:03:08.820
and a certain regularity
in the world, as Hume said,

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:12.780
a connection in the
world between two events.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.780
But the common view is
one and two don't depend

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.070
on the way the world is.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:24.210
They don't depend on any
regularity in the world.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:27.660
They depend on the way our language is,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.890
and the meaning of words,
and a conventional connection

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.270
between words in our language, CARNAP,

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.210
or on the language game

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:42.213
we happen to be playing, Wittgenstein.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:49.190
Now all three inferences,
the logical, the linguistic,

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:53.370
and the causal, guarantee the transmission

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.670
of truth from the premises to conclusion.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:59.130
That's why they are inferences.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.880
Indeed, they guarantee
the transmission of truth

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.350
in the world from premises to conclusion.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.560
Assuming the premises
are true in the world,

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.240
the conclusion is guaranteed
to be true in the world.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:20.220
But while the transmission of
truth in the causal inference

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:25.110
is due to a connection between
things or event in the world,

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:29.580
the transmission of truth
in the linguistic inference

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.660
is due to a connection
between words in our language,

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.610
bachelor and unmarried.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.330
And the view is the transmission of truth

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:43.773
in the logical inference
is also thought to be true

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.593
due to a connection between words.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:55.670
And this view, the correctness
of A is a bachelor,

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.900
therefore A is unmarried,
is due to a connection

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:05.900
between its non-logical
words, bachelor and unmarried,

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.810
and the correctness of
the logical inference,

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:14.810
Pa or Pb, not Pa, therefore
Pb, is due to a connection

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.013
between its logical words, or and not.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:24.660
But does this mean that one is grounded

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.813
only or mainly in language?

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.487
The sentence says in the inference,

00:05:31.487 --> 00:05:36.270
in the logical inference, say
something about the world.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.590
The first premise says that
in the world, at least one

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.140
of the two individuals, A and B,

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.470
is in P, or has the property P.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.770
The second premise says that in the world

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.830
A is in the compliment of P.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:57.393
And the conclusion says that
in the world, B is in P.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:03.270
Now the logical words or
symbols in this inference

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:07.500
could have meant something
different from what they mean.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.520
If negation meant affirmation,

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.180
the inference would not have been valid.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.180
But that would not change the fact

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:21.450
that in the world there is a connection

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:26.450
between at least one X and Y is in P,

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:32.240
and X is in the compliment
of P, and Y is in P.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.850
This is a connection in the world.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.000
And it is this connection in the world

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.030
rather than our linguistic conventions

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:45.360
or the language game we happen to play

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.360
that is responsible for the
logical validity of one.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:56.570
In this way, the logical
validity of Pa or Pb,

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:00.870
not Pa, therefore Pb, is similar in kind

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:05.870
to the causal validity of
A hit B, therefore B moved.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:11.510
They are due to certain
regularities that hold in the world.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:16.380
A causal regularity in the case of three.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:20.790
A formal regularity in the case of one.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:25.790
It is for this reason the truth
in the world is transmitted

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:30.890
from premises to conclusions
both in one and in two.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:37.380
So, not only are the
sentences of one and three

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:41.460
true or false in the
strong sense of being true

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:46.460
or false in the world,
their inferential power

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.560
is due to relevant regularities
or connections in the world.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:57.150
This is further seen by
the fact that no relevant

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:02.150
regularities or connections
exist in that when no relevant

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:07.320
regularities or connections
exist in the world,

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:12.320
the corresponding inferences are invalid.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:17.550
For example, since in the
world there is no regular

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:22.440
connection between billard
ball A being stationary

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:27.440
and billard ball B moving,
the inference A is stationary

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:34.490
therefore A is moving, is
invalid causal inference.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:41.040
Similarly, since in the
world there is no connection

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:46.040
between one, at least one
of X and Y being in P,

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:51.740
and X being in P, as you
can see in the picture,

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:58.880
and two, Y being in the complement of P,

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:04.230
the inference Pa or
Pb, this is a different

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:08.990
from the original, Pa, therefore not Pb

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.150
is not logically valid.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.200
It is a game.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.620
It could be an inferential
game, but it's not valid.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:20.553
There's nothing in the world
that connects the two parts.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:25.500
Let us see a case in which
accepting an inference

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:30.500
like 1 prime, that's Pa or
Pb, Pa, therefore not Pb.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:35.580
An influence that fails in the world

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:40.290
and acting upon it can bring
about death in the world,

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:43.260
and not just losing a game.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.870
Suppose A and B are mushrooms.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:48.300
P means poisonous.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.290
And in the world mushroom B is poisonous.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:55.170
This is compatible with the premises

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:59.280
of both the valid logical argument, one,

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:04.280
and the invalid game argument one prime.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:08.850
Pa or Pb, at least one is poisonous.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.280
And A is not poisonous.

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.230
We didn't say anything about A,

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:16.530
or A is poisonous being true.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:21.530
But while the game inference
one prime gives us license

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:26.070
to eat mushroom B, it
says it's not poisonous,

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:27.990
that will kill us.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:32.550
The worldly inference one does not.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:37.500
There is a life and death
difference between one

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.530
which is grounded in the world,

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:45.530
and one prime which is grounded
in a convention or a game.

00:10:46.530 --> 00:10:50.730
And the same holds in
other cases, just as using

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:55.140
an incorrect aerodynamic
laws in building an airplane

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:57.600
can cause the airplane to crash,

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:02.600
so using incorrect logical
laws in designing an airplane

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.980
can cause it to crash.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:09.540
Once I played a game of
creating a logic in which,

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.240
when you give instruction
lift you get drag,

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.040
when you give drag you get lift

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:16.983
because the logic tells you to do so.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:19.620
Conclusion.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:24.000
Logical inferences like
causal inferences are based

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.790
on regularities in the world.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:31.410
Physical regularities in the
case of causal inferences,

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:36.393
formal regularities in the
case of logical inferences.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:41.790
Two, counterfactual or modal scope.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:46.230
We have seen that logical and
causal inferences are similar

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:49.560
with respect to truth in the world.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:53.400
Next, let us turn to their counterfactual

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.683
scope or modal force.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:12:00.510
Inferences are divided
into weak, material,

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.643
and stronger, non-material.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:08.600
Weak, here we go from
premises to conclusion

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:13.350
and there's only very weak requirement.

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:17.520
It cannot be the case that
all the premises are true

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:21.210
and the conclusion is false,
where truth means true,

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:24.963
actually true in the
actual world, no more.

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:29.670
No requirement of
irregularity in the world

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:33.330
that connects the premises
to the conclusion.

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:37.560
For example, here is an example
of a material inference.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.750
San Diego is in California,

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:43.590
therefore New Haven is in Connecticut.

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:47.550
This is materially correct
because the consequence,

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:50.580
the conclusion is correct, is true,

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.820
and there's no regularity in the world.

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:57.030
That's material inference.

00:12:57.030 --> 00:13:01.200
Causal and logical
inferences are stronger.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:06.200
They require regularity,
indeed a stronger regularity,

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:10.950
one that includes counterfactual cases.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:15.543
Hence inferences have
counterfactual scope.

00:13:16.459 --> 00:13:21.459
Thus A hit B, therefore
B moved, holds not only

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:23.790
for actual billard balls

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:28.034
but also for counterfactual billard balls.

00:13:28.034 --> 00:13:33.034
Pa or Pb, not Pa, therefore
Pb holds not just for actual

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:39.030
mushrooms but also for
counterfactual mushrooms.

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:42.240
Both have counterfactual scope

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:45.090
but do they have the same scope?

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.133
And if not, why not?

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:52.440
I'm not looking for an answer
that relies on our intuitions.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.020
I usually don't believe in intuitions.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:59.550
I'm looking for a theoretically
systematic, precise,

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:02.610
informative, and correct answer.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:06.903
To arrive at such an answer
I return to invariance.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:12.270
And to make the answer more informative

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:14.880
I will move to new examples.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:18.540
In particular, I would
like to use an example

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:23.540
of a logical inference that
has a richer logical structure

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:26.940
and an example of a causal inference

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:30.720
that is related to a general law of nature

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.933
such as Newton's law of gravitation.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:40.880
My examples will be five,
for some X Px or not,

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:47.450
or QX, for all X, not Qx,
therefore for some X Px.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:54.510
Somewhat similar, but we
have here quantification.

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:58.740
Something is P or Q, nothing is Q,

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:00.843
therefore something is P.

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:06.810
Six, some kind of inference
from gravity to motion.

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:09.810
For example, gravity causes the free fall

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.903
of objects near the surface of the earth.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:19.040
I will show that five, the
logical inference is based

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:24.980
on a connection in the world
between properties that have

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:28.680
maximal degree of invariance

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:33.120
and this means that it
itself has a maximal

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:38.120
counterfactual scope, and that
means that it has a maximal

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:41.133
modal force that is necessity.

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:46.770
I will also show that
six, the causal inference

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:50.520
is based on a connection in
the world between properties

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:54.180
that have non-maximal invariance.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:58.530
Therefore they have non-maximal,
although significant,

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:03.530
counterfactual scope and
non-maximal, yet significant,

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:06.873
modal force or necessity.

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.600
Invariance.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:13.800
Invariance is a central topic
of interest both in science

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:16.260
and in logic and mathematics.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.720
There are many types of invariance.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:22.170
For example invariance of laws of nature

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:25.440
and the replacements
of frames of reference.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:29.850
Here I will focus on
invariance of properties

00:16:29.850 --> 00:16:33.423
and the replacements of individuals.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:38.280
To prevent misunderstanding,
let me clarify that

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:43.230
I use the term property
in its everyday sense,

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:48.000
not as a philosophical term
of art, such as universal,

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:52.140
and I'm also not interested
in the ontological status

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:53.970
of properties here.

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:57.930
What I say here is compatible
with different ontological

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.973
accounts of properties.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:05.870
Now, properties in general
are selective in nature.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:14.130
They distinguish between
some objects but not all.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:17.460
Example, the property is a human

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:21.270
distinguishes between me and my laptop,

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:25.320
but not between me and Alex,

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.890
or between my laptop and the number one.

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:31.500
Neither of them have this property,

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:33.693
so it doesn't distinguish between them.

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:38.310
The property is a woman does distinguish

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:43.310
between me and Alex, but
not between me and Priya,

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:46.173
or between Alex and the number one.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:52.840
I will say that is a human is invariant

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:55.980
and the replacements of me by Alex

00:17:55.980 --> 00:18:00.980
and of, say Mount Everest by
one, but not by a replacement

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:05.640
of me or Alex by one or Everest.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:10.320
In general, a first level
property P is invariant

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:13.830
under replacements of
individuals that have it

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:17.793
by individuals that have
it, and by individuals

00:18:17.793 --> 00:18:21.510
that don't have it by
individuals that don't have it,

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:24.450
but not by individuals that have it

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:28.053
by an individuals that don't have it.

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:32.610
So this is very general and simple.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:37.200
More precisely, I will talk
about invariance of properties

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:41.700
under one-to-one
replacements of individuals.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:46.700
Or if I take domains into
account under one-to-one,

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:50.610
and onto replacements of individuals.

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:53.733
For example in the domains,

00:18:55.890 --> 00:19:00.510
Gila, Alex, and the
number one, one domain.

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:05.510
And second, Pria, my
laptop, and Mount Everest,

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:09.840
Is a woman is invariant
under the one-to-one

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:14.840
and onto replacement R,
which goes from me to Priya,

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.880
and from Alex to my laptop,

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:20.610
and from Everest to the number one,

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:24.240
but not under the one-to-one
and onto replacement,

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:27.750
our prime, that goes from me to my laptop,

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:31.173
from Alex to one, and
from Everest to Priya.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:35.190
That is only a replacement
that lead us from things

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.220
that are women to things that are women,

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.643
or things that are not women
to things that are not women.

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:46.800
Now we are ready to proceed
to maximal invariance.

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:49.095
Maximal invariance.

00:19:49.095 --> 00:19:52.907
While the properties we
looked at so far are invariant

00:19:52.907 --> 00:19:56.546
under some are the properties...

00:19:56.546 --> 00:20:00.253
Okay, while the properties we
looked at so far are invariant

00:20:00.253 --> 00:20:03.660
under some one-to-one
and onto replacements,

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:06.360
they are not invariant under all.

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:10.740
But some properties are
invariant under all one-to-one

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:13.830
and onto replacements of individuals.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:17.343
These properties are maximally invariant.

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:22.080
Example, is identical to.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.840
Take any individual's, A B,

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:29.840
and replace them by any
individuals in a one-to-one manner.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:34.940
You replace A by RA and B by RB.

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:39.180
It is easy to see that
identity is preserved.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:44.180
A is identical to B if, and
only if, RA is identical to RB.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:50.850
If we have equinumerous domains,
this holds across domains

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:53.940
where R is one-to-one and onto.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:57.213
So identity is maximally invariant.

00:20:58.659 --> 00:21:03.480
The second level property non-emptiness

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:07.290
or non-empty is also maximally invariant.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:10.230
This property is the property denoted

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:12.960
by the existential quantifier.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:17.190
When we say. for some X PX, what we say is

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:21.470
that the property P is not
empty, so the denotation

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:24.600
of the existential quantifier
is the second level

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.943
property is non-empty.

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:31.890
Now take any two equinumerous domains,

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:36.890
D1 and D2, take any one-to-one
and onto replacement

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:39.783
R from D1 to D2.

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:46.020
Take any first level property P and D1,

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:50.930
and look at the image
of P, P prime under R.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:56.990
It is easy to see that
P is non empty in D one,

00:21:57.450 --> 00:22:01.620
If, and only if, its image
under one-to-one replacements

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:04.653
of the individuals is non empty in D2.

00:22:06.060 --> 00:22:11.060
So is non-empty is also
maximally invariant.

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:13.953
And we have the result, one.

00:22:15.090 --> 00:22:19.530
All the logical properties,
that is those that are denoted

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:23.970
by the logical constants such as identity,

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:27.000
complementation in a given domain denoted

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:31.650
by negation in a context like Px,

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:36.210
intersection, union,
inclusion, non-emptiness,

00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:40.290
and universality in a given domain,

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:43.740
they are all maximally invariant.

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:47.370
Second result, no physical properties

00:22:47.370 --> 00:22:49.083
are maximally invariant.

00:22:49.920 --> 00:22:54.870
One way to see that is to note
that they are not invariant

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:59.280
under one-to-one and onto
replacements of physical

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:02.610
individuals by mathematical individuals.

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:04.920
For example, numbers.

00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:07.290
All physical individuals are subject

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:09.360
to gravity but numbers are not,

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:14.043
and similarly for all
other physical properties.

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.010
Next result.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:22.010
Maximal invariance entails
large counterfactual scope

00:23:22.860 --> 00:23:25.863
which entails strong necessity.

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:32.780
Maximal invariance of
property entails stronger

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:38.180
counterfactual scope of
inferences based on them

00:23:39.090 --> 00:23:43.080
then of inferences based on non-maximally

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:45.750
invariant properties.

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:49.980
It follows from this
result, counterfactual scope

00:23:49.980 --> 00:23:54.510
of logical inferences is
greater than the counterfactual

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:58.230
scope of causal inferences.

00:23:58.230 --> 00:24:03.227
But the difference between them
is only a matter of degree.

00:24:05.070 --> 00:24:10.070
Now let me explain this, or
show that this is the case.

00:24:10.530 --> 00:24:14.850
Let us first explain this
result by means of an example,

00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:16.773
and then theoretically.

00:24:17.670 --> 00:24:22.050
The logical inference we
had before, for some X, PX

00:24:22.050 --> 00:24:27.050
or QX, for all X not QX,
therefore for some X PX,

00:24:27.510 --> 00:24:32.160
is logically valid because in the world

00:24:32.160 --> 00:24:37.160
the non emptiness, existential
quantifier, of the union,

00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:42.723
this junction, of two
properties and the emptiness

00:24:44.010 --> 00:24:49.010
of the second, for all X not, is connected

00:24:49.470 --> 00:24:54.000
by a formal regularity
to the non-emptiness

00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:56.640
of the first property.

00:24:56.640 --> 00:25:01.640
Now this holds in all
actual counterfactual

00:25:01.710 --> 00:25:05.100
domains of individuals,
that is in all domains

00:25:05.100 --> 00:25:09.543
of either actual or
counterfactual individuals.

00:25:12.180 --> 00:25:16.260
Therefore, the counterfactual
scope of this inference,

00:25:16.260 --> 00:25:19.623
hence its model scope, is very high.

00:25:21.210 --> 00:25:25.650
Another way to represent this
on the level of the world,

00:25:25.650 --> 00:25:29.970
the lowest level, where we look at actual

00:25:29.970 --> 00:25:33.810
and counterfactual individuals,
we have irregularity,

00:25:33.810 --> 00:25:38.070
a formal regularity or law,
non-emptiness of the union

00:25:38.070 --> 00:25:42.600
of P and Q, and emptiness of Q guarantees,

00:25:42.600 --> 00:25:47.550
or brings about, or
necessitates non-emptiness of P.

00:25:47.550 --> 00:25:52.020
This ensures that on the
level of truth, the truth

00:25:52.020 --> 00:25:56.610
of the two premises guarantees
the truth of the conclusion.

00:25:56.610 --> 00:26:01.610
And this guarantees that
the inference for some X, PX

00:26:01.680 --> 00:26:06.540
or QX for all X not QX,
therefore for some X PX

00:26:06.540 --> 00:26:09.180
is logically valid.

00:26:09.180 --> 00:26:12.540
This explains why the above inference

00:26:12.540 --> 00:26:16.290
transmits truth from
premises to conclusions,

00:26:16.290 --> 00:26:19.323
and does so with a strong necessity.

00:26:21.150 --> 00:26:25.650
A note on the scope of
maximally invariant properties

00:26:25.650 --> 00:26:27.873
and inferences based on that.

00:26:28.770 --> 00:26:32.700
Logical or formal properties
do not distinguish

00:26:32.700 --> 00:26:36.780
between individuals that
are physically possible

00:26:36.780 --> 00:26:38.820
and physically impossible.

00:26:38.820 --> 00:26:39.990
From their point of view,

00:26:39.990 --> 00:26:42.270
there's no difference between them.

00:26:42.270 --> 00:26:46.440
And even between individuals
that are metaphysically

00:26:46.440 --> 00:26:49.920
possible and metaphysically impossible.

00:26:49.920 --> 00:26:51.240
Example.

00:26:51.240 --> 00:26:54.240
From a formal or logical perspective,

00:26:54.240 --> 00:26:59.240
a ball that is both all red
and blue is just as possible

00:27:01.440 --> 00:27:06.440
and just as subject to formal
and logical regularities

00:27:06.510 --> 00:27:10.830
as a ball that is both all red and small.

00:27:10.830 --> 00:27:14.100
From the point of view of
the logical properties,

00:27:14.100 --> 00:27:18.480
there's no difference between
being all red and blue,

00:27:18.480 --> 00:27:20.490
and being all red and small.

00:27:20.490 --> 00:27:25.490
It simply doesn't, it abstracts
from all such differences.

00:27:26.100 --> 00:27:30.870
Therefore the counterfactual
scope of logical inferences

00:27:30.870 --> 00:27:35.553
includes individuals that
are both all red and blue.

00:27:37.680 --> 00:27:41.190
This is not the case
for causal inferences,

00:27:41.190 --> 00:27:44.850
which are based on connections
that apply to domains

00:27:44.850 --> 00:27:49.020
of actual counterfactual
physical individuals,

00:27:49.020 --> 00:27:53.340
but not to other kinds of individuals.

00:27:53.340 --> 00:27:54.690
Question.

00:27:54.690 --> 00:27:58.830
But how exactly is maximal
invariance connected

00:27:58.830 --> 00:28:00.663
to maximal necessity?

00:28:01.560 --> 00:28:02.970
Answer.

00:28:02.970 --> 00:28:07.500
If a property does not distinguish
between two individuals,

00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:11.430
the laws or regularities
governing or describing it

00:28:11.430 --> 00:28:14.760
cannot distinguish between them either.

00:28:14.760 --> 00:28:17.010
Otherwise, it'll not be a law

00:28:17.010 --> 00:28:19.920
or regularity of this property.

00:28:19.920 --> 00:28:24.720
They apply to one if, and only
if, they apply to the other.

00:28:24.720 --> 00:28:28.440
Now, if P is a maximally
invariant property,

00:28:28.440 --> 00:28:32.640
it does not distinguish
between any individuals actual

00:28:32.640 --> 00:28:36.630
or counterfactuals, where
the scope of counterfactual

00:28:36.630 --> 00:28:39.393
is broader than physical
counterfactuality.

00:28:42.600 --> 00:28:46.200
Therefore, the scope of
the laws or regularities

00:28:46.200 --> 00:28:51.200
governing describing TP is
also broader than the scope

00:28:51.960 --> 00:28:55.860
of physical laws regularities
and the inferences

00:28:55.860 --> 00:28:59.493
based on them are also very strong.

00:29:00.870 --> 00:29:04.020
Now, what about causal inferences

00:29:04.020 --> 00:29:07.740
and the laws regularities grounding them?

00:29:07.740 --> 00:29:12.210
Take the inferences be
from gravity to motion

00:29:12.210 --> 00:29:14.430
that we mentioned earlier.

00:29:14.430 --> 00:29:17.490
While the property is subject to gravity,

00:29:17.490 --> 00:29:22.490
some gravity, greater or smaller,
is not maximally invariant

00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:28.140
in the actual counterfactual
sphere associated

00:29:28.140 --> 00:29:31.290
with logical and formal properties.

00:29:31.290 --> 00:29:36.240
It is maximally invariance
in the smaller actual

00:29:36.240 --> 00:29:40.977
counterfactual sphere of
physically possible individuals.

00:29:40.977 --> 00:29:44.940
All physical individuals,
actual and counterfactual,

00:29:44.940 --> 00:29:46.653
are subject to gravity.

00:29:48.270 --> 00:29:52.860
In contrast, the property is a human,

00:29:52.860 --> 00:29:57.030
or is a homosapient, is
not maximally invariant

00:29:57.030 --> 00:29:59.250
in the physical sphere.

00:29:59.250 --> 00:30:04.050
For that reason, inferences
grounded in laws regularity

00:30:04.050 --> 00:30:07.230
governing or describing gravity

00:30:07.230 --> 00:30:12.230
have a stronger counterfactual
scope than inferences

00:30:13.830 --> 00:30:17.370
grounded in laws regularity governing

00:30:17.370 --> 00:30:20.283
or describing humanity.

00:30:21.210 --> 00:30:25.980
But weaker than logical
inferences, which are grounded

00:30:25.980 --> 00:30:30.930
in formal or logical
laws and regularities.

00:30:30.930 --> 00:30:35.640
So logical inference are
strongest, maximal invariance,

00:30:35.640 --> 00:30:37.350
maximally necessary.

00:30:37.350 --> 00:30:41.730
Physical inferences and physical
laws have a lower degree

00:30:41.730 --> 00:30:46.290
of invariance, lower degree of necessity.

00:30:46.290 --> 00:30:49.200
But they can still have
a significant degree

00:30:49.200 --> 00:30:52.080
of necessity such that the laws of gravity

00:30:52.080 --> 00:30:55.710
or inferences based on these regularities,

00:30:55.710 --> 00:30:59.730
and others too, can have
some counterfactual scope,

00:30:59.730 --> 00:31:01.353
but a smaller one.

00:31:02.370 --> 00:31:03.990
Conclusion.

00:31:03.990 --> 00:31:08.430
Both logical and causal
or physical inferences

00:31:08.430 --> 00:31:13.080
are grounded in certain
laws regularities that hold

00:31:13.080 --> 00:31:17.490
of some actual counterfactual individuals.

00:31:17.490 --> 00:31:22.140
Therefore both have a certain modal force.

00:31:22.140 --> 00:31:26.610
But due to the fact that
logical inferences are grounded

00:31:26.610 --> 00:31:31.530
in laws regularities that
govern or describe maximally

00:31:31.530 --> 00:31:35.340
invariant properties,
while causal inferences

00:31:35.340 --> 00:31:38.400
are grounded in laws regularities

00:31:38.400 --> 00:31:43.400
that govern or describe
non-maximally invariant properties,

00:31:45.210 --> 00:31:50.210
the counterfactual, hence modal
scope of logical inferences

00:31:50.730 --> 00:31:54.731
is greater than that of causal inferences.

00:31:54.731 --> 00:31:55.982
Thank you.

00:31:55.982 --> 00:31:58.982
(audience applauds)

00:32:01.520 --> 00:32:04.112
- [Announcer] We have
time for some questions.

00:32:04.112 --> 00:32:06.930
If there are questions from
people who haven't asked yet,

00:32:06.930 --> 00:32:08.880
I'll take those first.

00:32:08.880 --> 00:32:12.120
If not, please stand and-

00:32:12.120 --> 00:32:13.440
- [Participant 1] Yes,
thank you very much.

00:32:13.440 --> 00:32:15.930
I was wondering if you
could say something more

00:32:15.930 --> 00:32:20.930
about the counterfactual
mushroom, as an example.

00:32:21.297 --> 00:32:22.130
- Okay.

00:32:25.590 --> 00:32:27.030
The counterfactual,

00:32:27.030 --> 00:32:29.910
let me give you sort of a another example.

00:32:29.910 --> 00:32:32.250
I happen to have two children.

00:32:32.250 --> 00:32:35.130
Now, it is, I could have had three.

00:32:35.130 --> 00:32:38.100
And I could have said,
and there is a sense

00:32:38.100 --> 00:32:43.003
in which it is true to say
that my third counterfactual,

00:32:44.376 --> 00:32:48.180
the person who is the
third counterfactual child

00:32:48.180 --> 00:32:51.273
is a counterfactual child of mine.

00:32:52.650 --> 00:32:56.726
I think that in general when we talk,

00:32:56.726 --> 00:33:00.180
and we always talk about
counterfactual situations

00:33:00.180 --> 00:33:03.420
and counterfactual object,
counterfactual things.

00:33:03.420 --> 00:33:05.970
Should I build this
machine or that machine?

00:33:05.970 --> 00:33:07.830
If I build this one and not this,

00:33:07.830 --> 00:33:09.750
this is a counterfactual machine

00:33:09.750 --> 00:33:12.120
that maybe I could have built.

00:33:12.120 --> 00:33:16.260
Now I think that it's very
important to understand,

00:33:16.260 --> 00:33:21.260
to take into account
counterfactual objects

00:33:21.540 --> 00:33:24.600
when you want to understand properties.

00:33:24.600 --> 00:33:25.620
Why?

00:33:25.620 --> 00:33:30.210
First, for some properties you
they have different degrees

00:33:30.210 --> 00:33:33.810
of invariance, they distinguish
between different things

00:33:33.810 --> 00:33:35.370
and so there are difference.

00:33:35.370 --> 00:33:38.760
This is a significant
difference between them.

00:33:38.760 --> 00:33:42.240
But in the actual world they may not.

00:33:42.240 --> 00:33:45.510
I think Kelin likes the
example of has a heart

00:33:45.510 --> 00:33:47.760
and has a kidney, or something like this.

00:33:47.760 --> 00:33:51.330
It just so happens that
in the actual world,

00:33:51.330 --> 00:33:55.200
if we take into account
only actually individuals,

00:33:55.200 --> 00:33:57.630
they have the same invariances.

00:33:57.630 --> 00:34:00.900
But if you want to understand
the difference between them,

00:34:00.900 --> 00:34:02.463
you have to go beyond it.

00:34:03.360 --> 00:34:06.420
But even more than that,
if you take the property

00:34:06.420 --> 00:34:11.160
of gravity for example, in
order to understand gravity,

00:34:11.160 --> 00:34:16.160
we have to understand that
had earth had another moon,

00:34:18.450 --> 00:34:19.950
a counterfactual moon,

00:34:19.950 --> 00:34:23.250
it would also be subject
to gravity by earth.

00:34:23.250 --> 00:34:26.460
And we cannot understand gravity I think,

00:34:26.460 --> 00:34:29.280
well if we don't understand that.

00:34:29.280 --> 00:34:33.800
And so in general, in order
to understand properties,

00:34:35.040 --> 00:34:37.560
and then the laws that govern them,

00:34:37.560 --> 00:34:40.770
we have to understand
how they would behave

00:34:40.770 --> 00:34:45.030
if something that is not
the case, were the case.

00:34:45.030 --> 00:34:48.450
So that's where I get to
counterfactual objects

00:34:48.450 --> 00:34:50.973
and including a counterfactual mushroom.

00:34:53.691 --> 00:34:57.350
(Announcer speaking indistinctly)

00:34:57.350 --> 00:34:59.988
- [Participant 2] So in
in my everyday experience

00:34:59.988 --> 00:35:03.450
and at the experience of people I know,

00:35:03.450 --> 00:35:07.230
quite often inferences come after delay.

00:35:07.230 --> 00:35:08.940
You look at or work on something,

00:35:08.940 --> 00:35:11.250
think about something, nothing works.

00:35:11.250 --> 00:35:13.200
You wake up in the
morning, brush your teeth,

00:35:13.200 --> 00:35:14.730
and here's an answer.

00:35:14.730 --> 00:35:16.620
What mechanism does it involve?

00:35:16.620 --> 00:35:21.620
It's clearly not a causal,
or it's not language related.

00:35:23.040 --> 00:35:24.840
What mechanism involves there?

00:35:24.840 --> 00:35:26.520
And a broader question.

00:35:26.520 --> 00:35:29.970
I mean I appreciate this
logic, it's all logical,

00:35:29.970 --> 00:35:33.960
but what kind of mechanisms humans use

00:35:33.960 --> 00:35:36.780
to come up with inferences?

00:35:36.780 --> 00:35:39.750
- Okay, yeah. So I think
both the question you asked

00:35:39.750 --> 00:35:41.763
are for me, they are connected.

00:35:43.020 --> 00:35:46.290
I think that knowledge
in general depends both

00:35:46.290 --> 00:35:50.340
on how the world is, and
on how our mind works.

00:35:50.340 --> 00:35:54.420
We can only know the world
through the prism of our mind,

00:35:54.420 --> 00:35:57.780
of our cognitive resources.

00:35:57.780 --> 00:36:02.780
And so in the case of inferences
that you talked about,

00:36:03.630 --> 00:36:08.630
as a result of undergoing
this complex situation

00:36:09.060 --> 00:36:11.250
in which we both look in the world

00:36:11.250 --> 00:36:13.560
and use all our cognitive resources

00:36:13.560 --> 00:36:17.190
and come to know the
world better and better,

00:36:17.190 --> 00:36:21.840
we can see connections
between things in the world.

00:36:21.840 --> 00:36:26.840
And it is seeing the connection
between different things

00:36:26.880 --> 00:36:30.510
in the world that lead
us to make inferences

00:36:30.510 --> 00:36:32.370
about the subject matter.

00:36:32.370 --> 00:36:35.190
Sometimes the connection we see are formal

00:36:35.190 --> 00:36:39.090
and then the inferences will
be logical or mathematical.

00:36:39.090 --> 00:36:43.710
Sometimes the connection
we'll see is like a connection

00:36:43.710 --> 00:36:47.880
between taking aspirin
and fever going down.

00:36:47.880 --> 00:36:50.730
And then we will realize that in the world

00:36:50.730 --> 00:36:53.670
there's a connection
between certain components

00:36:53.670 --> 00:36:58.670
of these two phenomena,
and we draw an inference.

00:36:59.820 --> 00:37:04.020
And so generally, I
think, when we look at it,

00:37:04.020 --> 00:37:08.130
going to your second question,
how do we get to inferences?

00:37:08.130 --> 00:37:11.413
So, the way I look at it is this.

00:37:11.413 --> 00:37:14.820
I mean, human wants to
know the world as it is,

00:37:14.820 --> 00:37:17.883
but we have many limitations.

00:37:19.560 --> 00:37:20.820
We make mistakes.

00:37:20.820 --> 00:37:23.820
Our cognitive capacities are limited.

00:37:23.820 --> 00:37:26.550
So we need something that distinguishes

00:37:26.550 --> 00:37:29.310
between correctness and incorrectness.

00:37:29.310 --> 00:37:32.010
So, we introduce the concept of truth.

00:37:32.010 --> 00:37:36.450
And we also have limited time.

00:37:36.450 --> 00:37:41.110
We cannot always just
establish individually

00:37:42.420 --> 00:37:44.550
every statement we want to establish.

00:37:44.550 --> 00:37:48.930
So we look for shortcuts,
and inferences are shortcuts.

00:37:48.930 --> 00:37:53.070
In inferences, it's enough
to establish the premise

00:37:53.070 --> 00:37:56.700
and establish the
connection to other things.

00:37:56.700 --> 00:37:58.440
And then you get the conclusion

00:37:58.440 --> 00:38:02.490
and you don't have to
examine it separately.

00:38:02.490 --> 00:38:07.490
And I think that humans
have the ability to detect

00:38:10.170 --> 00:38:13.200
formal regularities in the world.

00:38:13.200 --> 00:38:17.580
For example, they can see,
if you take some physical

00:38:17.580 --> 00:38:20.940
properties, some properties are reflexive.

00:38:20.940 --> 00:38:23.370
That's a formal feature of a property.

00:38:23.370 --> 00:38:28.370
Some are symmetric, some are
transitive, some are not.

00:38:28.860 --> 00:38:33.860
And you can see that
if you have a property

00:38:37.590 --> 00:38:42.270
which is transitive, it
doesn't have to be symmetric.

00:38:42.270 --> 00:38:46.440
But if you have a property
which is both symmetric

00:38:46.440 --> 00:38:50.010
and reflexive and the universe is limited,

00:38:50.010 --> 00:38:52.290
you can get transitivity.

00:38:52.290 --> 00:38:57.290
And so we can figure
out formal connections

00:38:57.990 --> 00:38:59.220
between properties,

00:38:59.220 --> 00:39:02.280
we can figure out cardinality connections.

00:39:02.280 --> 00:39:07.280
We can say that for
example, the cardinality

00:39:07.590 --> 00:39:09.627
of people in this room
is maybe, I don't know,

00:39:09.627 --> 00:39:12.150
30, 40, something like this.

00:39:12.150 --> 00:39:14.550
Not zero, not 100.

00:39:14.550 --> 00:39:18.093
And we can draw connections between 40

00:39:18.093 --> 00:39:23.093
and cardinality 20 and say that the first

00:39:23.160 --> 00:39:25.980
is larger than the second, and so on.

00:39:25.980 --> 00:39:29.670
And so we observe
regularities in the world

00:39:29.670 --> 00:39:31.920
including formal regularities.

00:39:31.920 --> 00:39:35.640
And I think that's how we
get to logical inferences,

00:39:35.640 --> 00:39:38.340
and we observe regularities in general

00:39:38.340 --> 00:39:39.720
or connections in general,

00:39:39.720 --> 00:39:43.203
and that's how we get to
other kinds of inferences.

00:39:45.120 --> 00:39:46.650
- [Announcer] We can take one more.

00:39:46.650 --> 00:39:50.340
Naftali was first, and
then we will need to stop.

00:39:50.340 --> 00:39:53.190
But those of you who want to stay and talk

00:39:53.190 --> 00:39:54.840
a little bit more, we
have time before dinner.

00:39:54.840 --> 00:39:56.240
Naftali, (faintly speaking).

00:40:00.750 --> 00:40:03.420
- [Naftali] Yes, thanks
so much for your talk.

00:40:03.420 --> 00:40:05.940
So I like the notion
of maximal invariance,

00:40:05.940 --> 00:40:08.280
but I'm still having a really
hard time wrapping my head

00:40:08.280 --> 00:40:10.233
around formal irregularities.

00:40:12.240 --> 00:40:13.890
Especially the notion
of formal irregularities

00:40:13.890 --> 00:40:16.020
being something in the world.

00:40:16.020 --> 00:40:19.890
And maybe one way to put
the thing that I'm...

00:40:19.890 --> 00:40:21.690
Yeah sort of a bit bothered
by is you, you might think

00:40:21.690 --> 00:40:24.720
that actually maximum
invariance would actually

00:40:24.720 --> 00:40:27.060
count against formal
irregularities being in the world.

00:40:27.060 --> 00:40:28.800
I mean, the thought just
being is that if these logical

00:40:28.800 --> 00:40:30.930
truth could apply to a
totally fictional world,

00:40:30.930 --> 00:40:34.410
or even a world that's, you know...

00:40:34.410 --> 00:40:36.810
I mean it sort of seems to
take away from the notion

00:40:36.810 --> 00:40:40.290
that these are actually in
the world in some sense.

00:40:40.290 --> 00:40:41.850
So I dunno if I'm just
begging the question

00:40:41.850 --> 00:40:43.590
and you know, adopting what would take

00:40:43.590 --> 00:40:46.050
to be the more traditional
view about logical truths

00:40:46.050 --> 00:40:47.760
being true in virtue of form.

00:40:47.760 --> 00:40:52.440
But it still attracts me,
and maybe you could help me.

00:40:52.440 --> 00:40:55.110
- Okay, so first let me say something

00:40:55.110 --> 00:40:58.350
about formal irregularities in the world.

00:40:58.350 --> 00:41:01.440
First, perhaps I will
mention another result,

00:41:01.440 --> 00:41:05.103
which is an interesting
result, not obvious.

00:41:06.870 --> 00:41:11.870
It turns out that all higher
level mathematical properties

00:41:12.357 --> 00:41:15.120
are maximally invariant.

00:41:15.120 --> 00:41:19.800
But aside from identity and a few others,

00:41:19.800 --> 00:41:23.970
all first order, lower level
mathematical properties

00:41:23.970 --> 00:41:28.347
and mathematical individuals
are not maximally invariant.

00:41:29.400 --> 00:41:34.020
Now this is relevant to how
we think about the formal.

00:41:34.020 --> 00:41:37.380
Today we very often
think about the formal,

00:41:37.380 --> 00:41:39.900
the mathematical as first level.

00:41:39.900 --> 00:41:43.290
And we think about individuals 1, 2, 3,

00:41:43.290 --> 00:41:45.750
and we can say, well we have no evidence

00:41:45.750 --> 00:41:47.150
for their being in the world,

00:41:47.150 --> 00:41:51.120
and so we need to be Platonist
in order to accept that,

00:41:51.120 --> 00:41:52.260
and we don't want it.

00:41:52.260 --> 00:41:55.710
Let's just go with the
linguistic interpretation

00:41:55.710 --> 00:42:00.710
of mathematics and logic and so on.

00:42:02.310 --> 00:42:04.980
But now what I'm talking about

00:42:04.980 --> 00:42:08.760
is mostly properties of properties.

00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:11.850
Even if you start just
with physical individuals,

00:42:11.850 --> 00:42:13.140
you are human.

00:42:13.140 --> 00:42:18.003
And even you start just with
their physical properties,

00:42:19.020 --> 00:42:24.020
it is a fact that in the
same way that in this room,

00:42:24.210 --> 00:42:27.330
this room has the feature
that there are men in it

00:42:27.330 --> 00:42:28.653
and women in it.

00:42:29.550 --> 00:42:34.320
They also has the feature that
there are 40 humans in it,

00:42:34.320 --> 00:42:36.690
rather than a million or zero.

00:42:36.690 --> 00:42:37.950
It's just effect.

00:42:37.950 --> 00:42:41.490
And it's a formal fact
about the situation.

00:42:41.490 --> 00:42:46.490
It is a formal fact about the
relation of X sits next to Y,

00:42:49.740 --> 00:42:54.360
that this relation, which is
instantiated in this world,

00:42:54.360 --> 00:42:59.163
in this room, is symmetric
but not transitive.

00:43:00.450 --> 00:43:05.137
So it is sort of, there are formal facts.

00:43:05.137 --> 00:43:08.430
There are not on the level
of individual numbers

00:43:08.430 --> 00:43:09.990
and their properties.

00:43:09.990 --> 00:43:14.990
There are at the level of
largely second and higher level

00:43:15.450 --> 00:43:18.663
properties of physical
and other properties.

00:43:19.560 --> 00:43:24.180
Now, how do you reconcile
this higher level formality

00:43:24.180 --> 00:43:26.100
with the fact that we do mathematics,

00:43:26.100 --> 00:43:30.330
usually first level in terms
of individuals like numbers?

00:43:30.330 --> 00:43:34.120
My own explanation is, and
this is part of what I said

00:43:35.580 --> 00:43:39.000
before, how we know the world depends

00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:41.910
on our mind and on the world.

00:43:41.910 --> 00:43:46.260
It is very likely that
human beings are such

00:43:46.260 --> 00:43:50.010
that it's easier for them
to figure out relations

00:43:50.010 --> 00:43:52.590
between say, cardinality properties,

00:43:52.590 --> 00:43:56.010
when they think about them
in terms of structures

00:43:56.010 --> 00:43:58.320
of individuals and their properties,

00:43:58.320 --> 00:44:01.530
numbers and their properties,
rather than properties

00:44:01.530 --> 00:44:03.570
of properties of properties.

00:44:03.570 --> 00:44:08.430
That will explain why we talk
in terms of first order terms,

00:44:08.430 --> 00:44:12.150
which is very different to
connect them really to reality.

00:44:12.150 --> 00:44:14.700
But they are systematically correlated

00:44:14.700 --> 00:44:17.880
to these higher level terms, formal terms,

00:44:17.880 --> 00:44:22.080
that it's very easy to
connect them to reality.

00:44:22.080 --> 00:44:25.510
So that's how I sort of think that

00:44:26.535 --> 00:44:27.630
the formal is in the world.

00:44:27.630 --> 00:44:30.150
And I'll just say one more sentence.

00:44:30.150 --> 00:44:32.550
That even if you take the physical,

00:44:32.550 --> 00:44:35.910
I mean gravity is in
the world, even though

00:44:35.910 --> 00:44:38.730
it has certain counterfactual scope.

00:44:38.730 --> 00:44:43.260
So just because it holds of
counterfactual physical object

00:44:43.260 --> 00:44:45.360
doesn't mean that it's not in the world.

00:44:45.360 --> 00:44:48.540
I don't think about
counterfactual situations

00:44:48.540 --> 00:44:51.210
as other worlds or possible words.

00:44:51.210 --> 00:44:55.260
It's a way to represent
to ourself a certain force

00:44:55.260 --> 00:44:58.290
and a certain stability and generality

00:44:58.290 --> 00:45:00.300
that some properties have.

00:45:00.300 --> 00:45:01.893
So that's how I look at it.

00:45:04.472 --> 00:45:07.472
(audience applauds)

